config SPRD_IQ
	tristate "Spreadtrum IQ playback / I-Q data device"
	depends on OF
	depends on SPRD_SIPC
	depends on USB_F_VSERIAL
	help
	  Character device (/dev/iq_mem) exposing the reserved RAM region
	  shared with the protocol stack processor for I/Q playback and
	  modem data capture.

	  The region is named by the "sprd,region" phandle of the
	  "sprd,iq" device tree node and mapped through SIPC.  Data can
	  be pushed to the host over the vser USB bypass path, handed to
	  user space with mmap(), or moved by the modem straight into the
	  shared region; the mode is selected through the SET_MODE ioctl.

	  The driver only binds when the kernel command line contains
	  "androidboot.mode=iq"; on a normal boot it stays inert.

	  Port of the vendor 5.4 `sprd_iq.ko`.  Say M to build the module.
